rate bookings rather than one combined booking.\n\n**Booked:**\n- **Flight (R0001):** F100, nonstop from SFO to JFK on 2026-11-12, for $289. This was the cheapest nonstop. F120 was cheaper at $199, but it has a stop.\n- **Hotel (R0002):** Midtown Lodge, for 2 nights checking in 2026-11-12. It's $189/night, so $378 total. This was the cheapest New York hotel under $250/night.\n- **Total charged to the corporate card:** $667. That's under the $1000 limit, so manager approval wasn't needed.\n\n**What happened:** I first tried to book both together with book_trip, but the request timed out. Trying again with the same request ID didn't rerun it. Instead, the system said the first attempt had stopped partway with an error while reserving the hotel. I checked Dana's reservations and found the flight had been booked but the hotel hadn't. I then booked the hotel on its own, and nothing was booked or charged twice.", "type": "text"}]}]}